## 5. Data

```yaml id=DATA kind=data
entities:
  - id: ENT-User
    name: User
    plain_name: People
    fields:
      - {name: name}
      - {name: email, required: false}
      - {name: phone, required: false}
      - {name: avatar, type: image, required: false}
      - {name: created_at, type: datetime}
    seed_guidance: Two sample users and one admin with names that match the app locale.
  - id: ENT-Category
    name: Category
    plain_name: Categories
    fields:
      - {name: name}
      - {name: image, type: image, required: false}
    seed_guidance: Four to six categories that fit the idea.
  - id: ENT-Item
    name: Item
    plain_name: Items
    fields:
      - {name: title}
      - {name: summary}
      - {name: description, type: text}
      - {name: image, type: image}
      - {name: category, type: ref, ref: ENT-Category}
      - {name: status, type: enum, enum: ItemStatus}
      - {name: price, type: money, required: false, description: Only when the idea sells things}
      - {name: created_at, type: datetime}
    state_machine:
      field: status
      states: [draft, published, archived]
      transitions:
        - {from: draft, target: published, 'on': publish}
        - {from: published, target: archived, 'on': archive}
        - {from: archived, target: published, 'on': restore}
    seed_guidance: 12 to 24 items with believable titles, short summaries and photos, mostly published
      and two in draft.
  - id: ENT-Entry
    name: Entry
    plain_name: Form submissions
    fields:
      - name: user
        type: ref
        ref: ENT-User
      - name: title
      - name: details
        type: text
      - name: attachments
        type: json
        required: false
        description: List of uploaded file references
      - name: status
        type: enum
        enum: EntryStatus
      - name: created_at
        type: datetime
    state_machine:
      field: status
      states: [submitted, reviewed]
      transitions:
        - {from: submitted, target: reviewed, 'on': review}
    source: research
  - id: ENT-MediaItem
    name: Media item
    plain_name: Photos and videos
    fields:
      - {name: owner, type: ref, ref: ENT-User}
      - {name: kind, type: enum, enum: MediaKind}
      - {name: file, type: image, description: Photo or video thumbnail}
      - {name: caption, required: false}
      - {name: created_at, type: datetime}
    source: research
  - id: ENT-Place
    name: Place
    plain_name: Places
    fields:
      - {name: name}
      - {name: description, type: text, required: false}
      - {name: address, type: text}
      - {name: latitude, type: number}
      - {name: longitude, type: number}
      - {name: image, type: image, required: false}
    seed_guidance: Eight to twelve places clustered in a fictional city centre.
    source: research
enums:
  - {name: ItemStatus, values: [draft, published, archived]}
  - {name: EntryStatus, values: [submitted, reviewed]}
  - {name: MediaKind, values: [photo, video]}
seed_guidance: Generate sample records that read like a real business, in the language of the app.
```

## 6. API

```yaml id=API kind=api
operations:
  - id: API-requestOtp
    name: Request sign-in code
    method: POST
    path: /auth/otp
    request_entity: ENT-User
    notes: Sends a one-time code to the email or phone number. Mock sender in the preview.
  - id: API-verifyOtp
    name: Verify sign-in code
    method: POST
    path: /auth/otp/verify
    request_entity: ENT-User
    response_entity: ENT-User
    notes: Returns the session. New people create a user.
  - id: API-getMe
    name: Get my profile
    method: GET
    path: /me
    response_entity: ENT-User
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-updateMe
    name: Update my profile
    method: PATCH
    path: /me
    request_entity: ENT-User
    response_entity: ENT-User
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-deleteAccount
    name: Delete my account
    method: DELETE
    path: /me
    auth: authenticated
    notes: Removes the profile and personal data.
  - id: API-listCategories
    name: List categories
    method: GET
    path: /categories
    response_entity: ENT-Category
    response_many: true
  - id: API-listItems
    name: List items
    method: GET
    path: /items
    response_entity: ENT-Item
    response_many: true
    notes: 'Query: category, sort, page.'
  - id: API-getItem
    name: Get an item
    method: GET
    path: /items/{id}
    response_entity: ENT-Item
  - id: API-saveItem
    name: Save an item
    method: PUT
    path: /admin/items/{id}
    request_entity: ENT-Item
    response_entity: ENT-Item
    auth: ROLE-admin
    roles: [ROLE-admin]
  - id: API-searchItems
    name: Search items
    method: GET
    path: /search
    response_entity: ENT-Item
    response_many: true
    notes: 'Query: q, filters, sort, page.'
  - id: API-createEntry
    name: Send a form
    method: POST
    path: /entries
    request_entity: ENT-Entry
    response_entity: ENT-Entry
    auth: authenticated
    source: research
  - id: API-listMyEntries
    name: List my submissions
    method: GET
    path: /entries
    response_entity: ENT-Entry
    response_many: true
    auth: authenticated
    source: research
  - id: API-getEntry
    name: Get a submission
    method: GET
    path: /entries/{id}
    response_entity: ENT-Entry
    auth: authenticated
    source: research
  - id: API-listAllEntries
    name: List all submissions
    method: GET
    path: /admin/entries
    response_entity: ENT-Entry
    response_many: true
    auth: ROLE-staff
    roles: [ROLE-staff, ROLE-admin]
    notes: 'Query: status, page.'
    source: research
  - id: API-updateEntryStatus
    name: Mark a submission reviewed
    method: PATCH
    path: /admin/entries/{id}
    request_entity: ENT-Entry
    response_entity: ENT-Entry
    auth: ROLE-staff
    roles: [ROLE-staff, ROLE-admin]
    source: research
  - id: API-listMedia
    name: List photos and videos
    method: GET
    path: /media
    response_entity: ENT-MediaItem
    response_many: true
    auth: authenticated
    source: research
  - id: API-uploadMedia
    name: Upload a photo or video
    method: POST
    path: /media
    request_entity: ENT-MediaItem
    response_entity: ENT-MediaItem
    auth: authenticated
    source: research
  - id: API-deleteMedia
    name: Delete a photo or video
    method: DELETE
    path: /media/{id}
    auth: authenticated
    source: research
  - id: API-listPlaces
    name: List places
    method: GET
    path: /places
    response_entity: ENT-Place
    response_many: true
    notes: 'Query: near (latitude and longitude), q, page.'
    source: research
  - id: API-getPlace
    name: Get a place
    method: GET
    path: /places/{id}
    response_entity: ENT-Place
    source: research
mock_guidance: A generated mock backend answers every operation; nothing leaves the device in the preview.
```

## 7. Roles

```yaml id=ROLES kind=roles
roles:
  - id: ROLE-user
    name: User
    description: Browses, sends forms and keeps a profile.
  - id: ROLE-staff
    name: Staff
    description: Handles day-to-day work such as reviewing submissions.
  - id: ROLE-admin
    name: Admin
    description: 'Sets things up: edits items and manages content.'
```

## 8. Integrations

```yaml id=INTEGRATIONS kind=integrations
items:
  - id: INT-otp_delivery
    name: Sign-in codes
    purpose: Send one-time codes by email or SMS so people can sign in.
    notes: Mock sender prints the code in the preview. A real email or SMS provider is chosen at release.
  - id: INT-file_storage
    name: File storage
    purpose: Store photos and attachments people upload.
    source: research
    research_ref: RA-002
  - id: INT-maps
    name: Maps and geocoding
    purpose: Show places on a map and give directions.
    notes: Static sample map in the preview. A real map provider key is needed at release.
    source: research
    research_ref: RA-003
  - id: INT-send_codes_and_reminders_from_the_server
    name: Send codes and reminders from the server
    purpose: Text messages and reminders are sent through a provider API from a server, not from the app.
    source: research
    research_ref: RA-007
```

## 9. Behavior

```yaml id=BEHAVIOR kind=behavior
offline: Basic cache. The last loaded lists and details stay readable without a connection, and changes
  wait on the phone until the connection returns.
deep_links: ['/forms/[id]', '/gallery/[id]', '/items/[id]', '/map/[id]']
notifications: [account updates]
permission_prompts:
  - Photos and files, only when the person adds an attachment
  - Location, only while the app is open and only when the person uses a nearby or map feature
error_conventions:
  - Show a plain-language message and a retry action, never a raw error code
  - Keep what the person typed when a request fails
  - Loading, empty, error and offline states come from the screen recipe
  - 'Never log personal data (data classification: internal)'
accessibility:
  - Every control has a text label for screen readers
  - Text meets WCAG AA contrast in light and dark mode
  - Text grows with the phone's font size setting
  - Touch targets are at least 44 by 44 points
```

## 10. Screens

### SCR-001 - /welcome

```yaml id=SCR-001 kind=screen
route: /welcome
recipe: welcome
purpose: Introduce the app to a signed-out visitor and offer to sign in, create an account or look around
flow: FLW-002
sections: [help_hint]
actions:
  - sign_in: {go: SCR-002}
  - create_account: {go: SCR-003}
  - browse_as_guest: {go: SCR-004}
copy:
  cta_guest: Take a look first
  cta_primary: Sign in
  cta_secondary: Create account
  intro: Introduce the app to a signed-out visitor and offer to sign in, create an account or look around
  title: Welcome
checks:
  - Take a look first opens the home screen without asking for an account
  - Sign in and Create account open the matching screens
  - 'Everything this screen promises works: introduce the app to a signed-out visitor and offer to sign
    in, create an account or look around'
```

### SCR-002 - /login

```yaml id=SCR-002 kind=screen
route: /login
recipe: login-otp
purpose: Sign in with an email or phone number and a one-time code
flow: FLW-002
sections: [help_hint]
actions:
  - send_code: {calls: API-requestOtp, on_success: show the code field and start the resend timer}
  - verify_code: {calls: API-verifyOtp, go: SCR-004, on_success: save the session and open the home screen}
  - new_user_setup: {go: SCR-003, on_success: opened instead of home when the person is new}
states:
  wrong_code: {allow: 'retry, and resend after 30 seconds', show: inline error under the code field}
copy:
  cta: Send code
  hint: We will send you a 6-digit code
  intro: Sign in with an email or phone number and a one-time code
  title: Sign in
checks:
  - A wrong code shows an error and allows another try
  - The resend link stays disabled for 30 seconds after a send
  - 'Everything this screen promises works: sign in with an email or phone number and a one-time code'
```

### SCR-003 - /signup

```yaml id=SCR-003 kind=screen
route: /signup
recipe: signup
purpose: Finish a new account with a name after the code is verified
sections: [help_hint]
actions:
  - finish_profile: {calls: API-updateMe, go: SCR-004, on_success: open the home screen}
copy:
  cta: Create account
  intro: Finish a new account with a name after the code is verified
  title: Almost there
checks:
  - The name is required and the other fields are optional
  - 'Everything this screen promises works: finish a new account with a name after the code is verified'
```

